bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    engine2d_plain_text_inherits_selected_face_2026-11-28, 0, "A Draw IR text command with no font-identity (an input's value run) goes to Engine2D draw_text, which paints with whatever face the previous text command selected (font_owner.active), also across frames, and with the 5x7 bitmap face otherwise. So the run's raster depends on what was painted before it. Seen on the page of direction_rtl_bidi_order_chrome159_spec with the value command emitted before the div text: the CPU frame inks rows 53..58 where the Vulkan frame inks 52..58 (132 px differ)."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    engine2d_plain_text_inherits_selected_face_2026-11-28, P2, open, "engine2d: a text run without a font identity paints with the previously selected face", src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/engine2d/draw_ir_adv.spl, 3192, "emit the input value text command of direction_rtl_bidi_order_chrome159_spec before the div text commands; AC-6 (Vulkan frame equals CPU frame) fails", 2026-11-28, 2026-11-28, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    engine2d_plain_text_inherits_selected_face_2026-11-28, 0, "2026-11-28 float-paint-order lane: found, not fixed (the input value glyph path is held on work/webrender-input-value-glyph-held-20261122). Workaround in _html_draw_ir_node_paint_order: a form control box is listed with the inline content (scope_inlines) in tree order where CSS 2.1 Appendix E puts a block-level control in Step 4. Real fix: give the value run its own face (font-identity) or make the plain path select the default face; then drop the form-control test."
